;; S30, S33, QDS-18, QDS-19, OQP-16 & Issue F50 (25,000 trials):
;; Persistent Okasaki DAG Shared-Node Physical-Wire Aliasing & Symmetric Lens Container
;; - Issue F50 (`GAP-2`): When a persistent Okasaki tree/deque shares a DAG sub-node
;;   across two branches (`left` and `right` children aliased to overlapping physical
;;   wires), lowering `c-with-uncompute` applies a controlled gate whose control and
;;   target masks overlap `(bitwise-and control-mask target-mask) != 0`, triggering a
;;   self-aliasing unitary fault!
;; - Verifies `QDS-19` (`polynomial-functor-lens-container`), `S30` (`s30-dag-uniqueness-borrow-disjointness`),
;;   `QDS-18` (`catenable-realtime-deque`), `S33`, and `OQP-16` (`oqp16-catenable-deque-window-sliding-qft`).
